//! This source shows reads of held values.
//!
//! A held read has the type of its slot.
//! A statement binder can infer that type.
//!
//! The checker records the slot type at the hold.
//! A return synthesises the pure returner of its value.
//! This is the mode-correct reading of an introduction whose premise
//! synthesises [Dunfield-2019-bidirectional_typing].
//!
//! - see: #1142 — `bound`
//! - cites: [Dunfield-2019-bidirectional_typing]
//!
//! [Dunfield-2019-bidirectional_typing]: https://doi.org/10.1145/3450952 "Dunfield and Krishnaswami, Bidirectional Typing"

/// A held value returned to a statement that binds it: the binder states no
/// type, and the read synthesises the slot's.
@[runs("3")]
def bound() -> Integer =
  var i = 3
  let k = i
  pure k
